@flexiarg test-registry/spot-check-at-the-declared-rate
@title Spot-Check At A Declared Rate, And Say What A Spot-Check Can Show
@keywords sampling, spot-check, declared-rate, tamper, drift, prior, confidence
@audience reviewers, lane-policy authors
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-16 (claude-7; Joe's ruling 2026-09-14: one test per routine review by default, re-priced on measurement; zai-8's countercheck futon2 runs/cascade-worked-example-2-2026-09-15)
@references [test-registry/judge-adequacy test-registry/rerun-when-the-warrant-fails test-registry/meter-the-saving hygiene/classify-by-remedy-judgement translation/test-by-reproducing-behaviour]
@see-also buffer-cleaner/classify-staleness
@how in the routine lane, after a passing record check, execute exactly one declared test from the warrant (reviewer's choice, recorded) and confirm it executed one test and agrees with the recorded result. Its role is a drift and tamper check on the record — does this environment reproduce what the record says — not a correctness verdict. The rate is a declared value with its source, re-priced when measured disagreement rates exist.
@violation-signature a spot-check reported as evidence of correctness; a sampled test not recorded; a "spot-check" that runs the whole namespace; a rate changed without a measurement.
! conclusion: A routine review executes one recorded, declared test to check the record reproduces; its result is evidence about the record, not about correctness.

  + context: A warrant has passed its record check in a routine lane.

  + IF:
    The reviewer wants some execution evidence without repeating the run.

  + HOWEVER:
    One draw carries little information about a sparse bug, so treating it as a verdict overclaims; and never executing anything makes a tampered or non-reproducible record undetectable.

  + THEN:
    Run one declared, recorded test at the declared rate as a reproduction check.

  + BECAUSE:
    The complete record decides correctness for deterministic tests; the spot-check keeps the record honest.

  + evidence: zai-8 FINDING (futon2 b9b3047c predeclaration; 40/40; 0.5263); zai-7's 2026-09-14 spot-check: one test, one assertion, 902 ms.
